# Mock-first dashboard mode — Observe screens (W1) read shared seeds.
# Unset / empty defaults to mock=true (fresh checkout, test run, `bun run dev`
# all render seeds without a host running beside them). Real mode is opt-in:
# set VITE_USE_MOCK=false AND VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:17173 to
# point generated hooks at the host. Without VITE_API_BASE_URL, kubb-client
# will refuse to call the backend on first request.
VITE_USE_MOCK=true

# Dev URL is fixed: http://localhost:17173 (Comuki port pool — ports.md)
# Do not override Vite port via CLI; vite.config.ts uses strictPort.

# Mock-only run: use `bun run dev:mock`.
# `bun run dev` fires the `predev` hook first (dotnet build + kubb generate),
# which regenerates the API client from OpenAPI — needed when the contract
# changed, pointless and slow when the screens are serving seeds.

# Where the platform's own source lives — the topbar's repository link.
# Defaults to this repository, so a fresh checkout needs no line at all.
# Set it to a fork's address to repoint the link, or to the empty string
# (`VITE_REPO_URL=`) to take the link out of the bar. Only http/https pass;
# anything else is read as "no link".
VITE_REPO_URL=https://github.com/dot-stbl/comuki

# Real-mode OIDC: name of the provider the host is configured for (the value
# must match one of the names listed under `[auth.providers.*]` in the host's
# TOML). Unset or empty → the "Continue with …" button is hidden in real
# mode. Mock mode ignores this — the mock store's `setMockOidcProvider` is
# authoritative there.
# VITE_OIDC_PROVIDER=comuki
